Lisa has always protected Kyle, to the point where she protected Kim as well because it was upsetting Kyle for her not to (this was in the earlier seasons). Lisa protected Brandi during her stoush with Adrienne, even though it would've been in her best - and her businesses' best - interests for her not to. Lisa paid off Stassi's blackmailer on VPR when it would've been great free publicity for her show if the tape had've leaked (which unfortunately it later did). Lisa offered to put Taylor up and help her in any way possible to get her away from Russell, and that was while saying that she wasn't doing it to just seem like a good person ("I'm not coming in here masquerading as your best friend"). 

&amp;#x200B;

Manipulative or not, Lisa does more to protect others than Kyle - who does not return the favour - and is more of a charitable and generous person. Kyle's entire 'career' is off her own self aggrandisement, including her awful TV show and fashionable line of moumous.

Yeah, I feel like there was a level of preplanning in it on Kyle's behalf. It's eerily similar to the way she calls out LVP this season. Like, she's convicted in her statements and ready to just go in and continue going on until she gets the response that she wants on camera. I feel like Adrienne was in on it too. 

&amp;#x200B;

There's real venom and hatred there towards Kim, who is genuinely scared and disoriented. There's something really heartbreaking about when Kyle advances on Kim physically and Kim hides behind Adrienne immediately. You can tell Kim is no stranger to domestic violence and, even if Kyle wouldn't go there (that'd be a pretty big accusation), it's still cruel to come after someone who is obviously traumatised and get into their physical space like that.

I guess the point I'm trying to get to is the one Billie Lee makes herself, "I don't think the girls are transphobic. I think they're self involved and unaware." For me, that puts a finer point on it than just dismissing them as transphobic - I don't think they care about Billie Lee being trans as much as they feel threatened by a new castmate, and what they're doing is very similar to past new girls too. They're catty, mean and shitty to work with - they make the environment hostile - but it's not because she's trans. 

&amp;#x200B;

Katie overall is just a total cunt. Sorry, there's not another word for her. She bullies and belittles even those close to her and of course she's unpleasant to new comers because she's a fairly irrelevant cast member. Her "not my problem" proves Billie's point - it's not that Katie *hates* that Billie's trans, she is so self absorbed with the perceived threat of being *called* transphobic that she now refuses to sympathise with someone who has had a painful journey towards self-identity. Which isn't inherently transphobic. It's just cunty. 

&amp;#x200B;

But I also understand that at this point I'm doing the classic Reddit thing where I'm splitting hairs unnecessarily, so feel free to disagree.

Such a strange and wild turn of events. 100% my favourite moment in any documentary. 

&amp;#x200B;

"Killed them all, of course."

I honestly think Scheana is trying to back-door-pilot her way into a Relationshep style bachelorette show. Hence all the weird scenes where she's on dates with ex-Bahelorette rejects (BLEAK) and being 'unlucky in love' with Adam, who is too much of a block of wood to give her literally anything back. 

&amp;#x200B;

Scheana has always lacked charisma to me - that's my perception of her, at least - and I think shes actually a fairly sweet, if self-absorbed, girl who just isn't great TV.

I've just got to vent for a second y'all how pathetic Randell's response has been. It's the most mewling, pissweak, grovelling string of texts, with a weird ploy that Fofty might make him have a heart attack if he doesn't stop putting him on blast. Like you're talking to a guy who got shot 9x and you're telling him your frail heart can't take a roasting? No. 

&amp;#x200B;

Also being like "pls now my ex is involved"  is SO. LAME. And high school! What is this mentality!
